Z||000139||84Bill||06-21-2001||12:30 PM||||I hate those things!<BR>Let me tell you a story. See about a year ago I went and got a new one to replace the one I've had since 1985. So I sit in the seat and commence chopping with the axe. Well 3 hours later a busted windshield 2 holes in the dash, a cracked rearview and an hour wait on hold with ASPLUNDA, all I managed to do was frey the edges on the stupid thing. So I decided it was best just to leave it there and spray pinesol on it. I recently sold the new one for 35 bucks on ebay and vow never to get another one.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000140||Fiero5||06-21-2001||12:32 PM||||The wind was moaning thru the cold fall air, and the leaves were rustling in swirls accross the ground. You could hear footsteps crunching on the brittle leaves, as someone approached.<BR>Four teenagers walked up the dark path on that fatefull Halloween night, crossing into a used car lot. They notice a nice looking red Pontiac Fiero sitting kinda lonely in the back of the lot. They wander over to the nice looking sports car, and decide to take a moment to check it out. "My Dad had one of these once". responds Todd, a tall limber young man. Bill turns to him, "I never saw your Dad with a Fe-air-o before", he says in a drawl. "Yup, had one just like this actually, right down to the same kinda rims it looks like", answers Todd as he wipes off some leaves from the hood. <BR>"Well, what happened to it since I never saw it?" asks Bill. <BR>"Well, there was an accident in it. It was quite a few years ago before some you guys moved to town. My Dad had just purchased it, and that night he let my uncle take it for spin down around the old grave yard. My uncle never came back"<BR>"Well, what your Dad do?" asked Betty.<BR>He called the Sheriff and they went looking for him.". <BR>Nancy looks up from the car, "So what did they find?" she asks. <BR>"They found the car sitting down near the opening to the cemetary, and my uncle was gone. He had bumped into the stone wall near the entrance I guess, but nothing major." Bill turns and looks over the back near the large spoiler. Todd turns to Nancy to see what she is looking at. Betty starts to look a bit cold as she walks over near Todd. "Where did your uncle go?" she asks. "Vanished without a trace." answers Todd. "They never found him. The only odd thing I heard about was they found this green air freshener on the ground near the drivers door." adds Todd.<BR>"Wow, that is kinda creepy" responds Nancy, as she then tries to peer into the passenger window.<BR>"What's so odd about that?, asks Bill. "Lot's of cars have those silly things". <BR>Todd circles around the front of the Fiero and notices that the nose has a bit of a dent in it. As he leans over to take a closer look, he blinks his eyes in amazement. The bumper seems to be repairing itself. It slowly pops out and at the same time, the paint webbing and chipping seems to vanish. He quickly turns to his girlfriend who is checking out the interior thu the passneger window, "Betty, did you see that?". <BR>"See what?" she asks.<BR>Just then Bill acts like he is choking, and the two girls rush over to him. Bill seems to have his arms up at his throught. Todd looks up to see what all the commotion is about. "What the hell are you two doing?" he asks as it looks like the girls are grabbing his neck and yanking on him. Todd rushes over and suddenly he sees the trouble. Bill has a little black string tightly wrapped around his neck. "He...l..p!" coughs Bill. Todd quickly steps up to help. He reaches up and tries to get his fingers under the tight string, to try and get some slack so Bill can get some air. Suddenly Todd feels something worming it's way up his arm. He notices that it seems to be attached to the black string he is grabbing. Suddenly, there it is!! To Todd's horror, a green air freshener inches it's way up his arm. It seems to turn at him, and then he hears this low growling devilish voice say..."I'm baaaaack".<P>Aaaahhhh!!! Will the horror never end???<P>Stay tuned next week for the thrilling conclusion to: "The air freshener from the dead".<P>Steve Kelley productions<BR>in assoction with 20th century foxes||||reg||11
