Z||000146||Fiero5||06-22-2001||03:50 PM||||.....It seems to turn at him, and then he hears this low growling devilish voice say..."I'm baaaaack".<P>Aaaahhhh!!! Will the horror never end???<P>And now the thrilling conclusion to: "The air freshener from the dead".<P>Bill's eyes were starting to roll up into the back of his head, as the string was strangling him to death. The girls tried to hold him up while grabbing at the string, but with no air to breath Bill was going unconsious. Todd was frozen in fear as the Air freshener seemed to be starring at him.<BR>Todd had been able to get his fingers of one hand under a bit of the string. His fingers were now turning purple as the string was pulling tighter and tighter. Suddenly Todd felt a sharp pain on his face as Betty slapped him hard. "Snap out of it damn it!" she screamed. Todd shook his head to clear the cobb webs. Todd then realized he was getting pulled down as Bill was collapsing to the ground. Todd quickly reached into his back pocket with his free hand and pulled out his pocket knife. He grabbed the notch on the blade with his teeth and pulled the blade out. Quickly but carefully he starts to cut the string near where it starts to wrap around Bills neck. Suddenly, Todd feels a funny touch on his own neck. He looks down and  notices another string coming out from the bottom of the air freshener and slowly moving up and around his own neck.<BR>"Betty!" he yells, "My neck!".<BR>Betty runs over and let's out a blood curdling scream as she see's the string begining to swirl around Todds neck.<BR>Betty grabs at the string to try and stop it from making it all the way around.<BR>"Just keep it busy for a few more seconds", yells Todd.<BR>Nancy realizes that the air has gotten colder as she see's her own breath now, and the wind has picked up significantly. Nancy looks up as she watches the leaves getting blown around, swirling into a small circle over parts of the ground.<BR>"Todd, the wind is getting stronger!" she yells.<BR>Todd hears her but is busy trying to cut the rest of the string off from Bills neck. The string is fraying, but Todd can't seem to get the rest to let go. He digs in a bit with his knife, gouging Bills neck enough to break the skin. <BR>Finally, the string gives way and Todd falls backward knocking Betty over as well. The air freshener flips up and lands on the ground about 15 feet away from them, but quickly leaps back towards the two fallen teenagers.<BR>Todd quickly get's to his feet and grabs Betty. he yanks her up and they run back towards their two freinds. Todd looks back quickly and see's that the air freshener is right on their heels. Todd looks up and see's Nancy standing right in their path.<BR>Todd smiles, "Make it a good one", he yells and then shoves Betty off to the side as he then leaps to his left. Nancy, having found an old shovel now has it raised in the air over her head and takes aim at the on coming air freshener.<BR>Todd rolls on the ground and then turns in time to see Nancy bring the shovels metal head down right onto the devilish air freshener..<BR>"Wang!" goes the shovel as Nancy slaps the metal shovel hard to the ground with all her might.<BR>Todd races back over as nancy picks up the shovel ready to give it another good smacking.<BR>But as she lifts the shovels head, their is no sign of the air freshener.<BR>"Did I miss?" she asks with tears in her eyes.<BR>The three teenagers turn and look in all directions. The wind is now really howling and the leaves are starting to be like sharp projectiles flying about at the teenagers.<BR>"Let's get the hell outa here!" yells Todd over the loud groan of the wind and rustling leaves.<BR>Todd and Betty grab Bill and help him up off the ground. Bill looks up and smiles at his friends as they then head for the path.<BR>"Todd!" yells Nancy, "Look!".<BR>Todd turns back and his eyes grow large in fear. He see's a small cyclone of wind and leaves swirling up into the air growing larger by the second.<BR>"Come on!" yells Todd, as Nancy then decides to get moving. She picks up to a dead run and catches up with her friends quickly as they are still helping Bill to get going.<BR>"It's catching up to us", hollars Nancy as she helps grab Bill and pull him along. Bill finally gains enough breath to be able to start running on his own.<BR>Todd notices out of the corner of his eye that the edge of the air cyclone is now right behind them.<BR>"What is it?" cries Betty as they pass the gate to the car lot and quickly head out onto the old dirt road.<BR>"I don't know, but let's try and make it to the old Barnaby house up the street." yells Todd.<BR>"No" responds Bill, "That house has been condemned after the Murders happened there."<BR>The wind howls  and leaves are starting to sting the teenagers legs and arms as the swirling cyclone seems to be following them up the street.<BR>"That was years ago" says Todd as they reach the walkway to the house. "Besides, that's all hogwash anyway!" he snaps.<BR>Winded, the four teenagers jog up the long stone walkway to the large old mansion.<BR>Todd get's to the stairway, and he leaps up every other step and quickly reaches the porch before his friends. As the groaning wind fills the air, Nancy looks back to see a cluster of leaves forming a shape. She is sure it looks like it is forming a siluette of a human being, but she then stumbles a bit on the rough stoneway so she turns back to watch where she is going.<BR>Todd reaches the front of the doorway and falls against the door grabbing the knob and frantically turning it. Then Bill and Betty stumbling accross the top of the porch out of breath crash into Todd shoving him against the door. The door gives way as a dust cloud wisks out from the opening, as if the door had been sealed for years. Nancy reaches the porch and quickly heads for the now opened doorway.<BR>Todd and Bill swing around the door and get ready to close it as Betty passes them through the door way. Nancy is right behind her and falls thru the doorway. Todd and Bill waste no time pushing the large creeping door back shut again with what strength they have left.<BR>They then hear a screaching sound from behind the now large closed door, as the wind hits the front of the house in a big gush.<BR>The house creeks and groans against the weight of the wall of wind hitting the front dead on.<P>We will be right back after a word from our sponsors.<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000147||fierohoho||06-23-2001||06:12 PM||||I don't get it. <P>If your cars stink, clean em. <P>If it's you take a bath/shower. <P>If I see more than one in a car I wonder "what smell are they trying to cover up?", thats why I call more than one a "Felony Forest". <P>Now quit wasting time here and go back to the other big thread where world problems are being solved. <P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
